  "_about": "Component spec for pos-password (docs/inspect refactor, component migration batch, 2026-08-26). Single source of truth for the Variants/Usage/Tokens tabs on /style-guide \"Password input\" section. Reuses the already-curated usage prose from COMP_CONFIGS['password'].usage and token data from the existing inspect-password.liquid (verified-accurate, currently-live data) restructured into the new schema. Single representative variant — this component's preview shows one instance (no Variant/Base toggle needed per the 2026-08-25/26 \"multiple sub-variants side by side\" rule). Regenerate the spec partial with the script in RULES.md 6.4 if the source data changes; do not hand-edit token values here. Updated 2026-08-27: the strength meter Inactive bar token corrected from --pos-color-frame (resolves to white in HC mode, invisible against a light background) to --pos-color-content-icon-disabled (a real grey in every theme) — matches the pos-forms.css fix. Updated 2026-08-27: added usageExample/props/composedOf (Target architecture point 1 fields that were left empty when this spec was first generated).",
  "component": "password",
  "name": "Password input",
  "description": "Collecting a password, PIN, or any value the user should not see while typing.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Collecting a password, PIN, or any value the user should not see while typing.",
    "The input must allow the user to toggle visibility — always provide the show/hide toggle."
  ],
  "whenNotToUse": [
    "Collecting non-sensitive text — use a regular text input instead.",
    "The value does not need to be hidden — a masked input creates unnecessary friction."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Always provide a show/hide toggle so users can verify their input.",
    "Use the strength meter on registration and password-change forms — it gives immediate feedback.",
    "Pair the strength meter with a strength description for screen readers (<code>aria-live</code> on the description)."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "Hide the show/hide toggle — users who type on mobile need it most.",
    "Show the strength meter on login forms — it is irrelevant and distracting there.",
    "Use <code>autocomplete=\"off\"</code> — this breaks password managers and reduces security."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "The show/hide toggle must have a meaningful <code>aria-label</code> or <code>title</code> (e.g. \"Show password\").",
    "The strength meter description uses <code>aria-live=\"polite\"</code> so screen readers announce strength changes.",
    "Password input should have <code>autocomplete=\"current-password\"</code> on login forms and <code>autocomplete=\"new-password\"</code> on registration forms."
  ],
  "composedOf": [],
  "props": [
    {
      "name": "pos-form-password-strength-{1,2,3}",
      "type": "class on .pos-form-password",
      "default": "none (0)",
      "description": "Set via JS as the user types — 1=Weak, 2=Medium, 3=Strong. Omit the strength meter/description elements entirely if not needed (e.g. login forms)."
    }
  ],
